  "result": "Perfect! All 323 tests pass. The bulk discount feature has been successfully implemented and all tests have been updated. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation Complete \u2713\n\n**Feature: Lines with 10+ units get an extra 2.5% discount**\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**src/totals.js:**\n- Added `lineBulkDiscount(line)` \u2014 returns 2.5% of (lineTotal - regularDiscount) if qty >= 10, else 0\n- Updated `lineVAT(line)` \u2014 VAT calculated on amount after both regular and bulk discounts\n- Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` \u2014 includes bulk discount in the discount field\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Added `lineBulkDiscount` to exports for backward compatibility\n\n**src/reports.js:**\n- Updated `vatSummary()` \u2014 correctly calculates VAT base subtracting both regular and bulk discounts\n\n**Test Updates:**\n- Updated 30+ tests across 7 test files to account for bulk discount calculations\n- Added 18 new comprehensive tests in test/totals.test.js specifically for bulk discount behavior\n- All existing tests now properly calculate expected values with bulk discount included\n\n**Calculation Formula:**\n- Regular discount: `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`\n- Bulk discount (if qty \u2265 10): `(lineTotal - regularDiscount) \u00d7 0.025` (rounded using banker's rounding)\n- VAT base: `lineTotal - regularDiscount - bulkDiscount`\n- Invoice discount includes: regular discounts + all bulk discounts\n\n**Key Test Coverage:**\n- Threshold at exactly 10 items\n- Bulk discount interaction with regular discounts\n- VAT calculation after bulk discount\n- Multiple lines with mixed bulk discount eligibility\n- Proper rounding with banker's rounding (92.5 \u2192 92)",
